nBeyer & Pritchett","ends":"2026-11-02T16:30:00-07:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued October 31 at 10:37AM MDT until November 2 at 12:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow expected above 10, 000 feet. Total snow\naccumulations between 12 and 18 inches, with locally higher amounts\npossible. Winds gusting as high as 45 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Northwest San Juan Mountains and Southwest San Juan\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 AM Sunday to noon MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult to impossible. The\nhazardous conditions will impact the Monday morning commute.","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2bdd41b860e09ab541155db973dc91e9b1c8543e.001.2","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2bdd41b860e09ab541155db973dc91e9b1c8543e.001.2"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 30 at 3:02PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and southeast\nUtah, including the following areas, Canyonlands/Natural Bridges,\nLa Sal and Abajo Mountains and Southeast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...From late Saturday night through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recently burned areas, and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1 to 3 inches of rain is expected across portions of southeast\nUtah and southwest Colorado from Sunday morning through Monday\nmorning over soils that are still saturated from recent rainfall\nand flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d9e2fd526e1e61f9532cd34833bc42a40d097b54.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d9e2fd526e1e61f9532cd34833bc42a40d097b54.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-31T23:11:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 312311 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 511 PM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flooding/flash flooding concerns increase Sunday into Monday, especially for areas that have saturated soils from last week's rain. A Flood Watch remains in effect. - Forecast river responses have increased, with a number of gages in southwest Colorado exp","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-31T18:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-011000- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1236 PM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI